<Page title="Affiliate Disclosure | MySpaFilter" description="How MySpaFilter labels Amazon, FiltersFast and Doheny's links, and the Associates tag those Amazon links use.">
<h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
<p><strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong></p>
<p>Some links on MySpaFilter go to retailers, including Amazon, FiltersFast and Doheny's. If you buy something after clicking one, we may earn a commission. You do not pay extra. The commission does not change which cartridges are in the cross-reference, which number we print, or which rows we mark unverified. Part numbers come from the cited catalogs whether or not a retailer pays us. That rule is also in the <a href="/about/#funding">about page</a> and the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
<h2>How the links are marked</h2>
<p>Every retailer link uses <code>rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"</code> and opens in a new tab. Pages that contain an Amazon link also show a short disclosure next to the buttons: “As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.” A site-wide line at the top of every page says the same thing and links here. Guides that discuss a specific part add an Amazon search for that part number. Cartridge pages add retailer buttons for the part on the page.</p>
<h2>Amazon: this site’s tag only</h2>
<p>Amazon links on this site use the Associates tag <strong>myspafilter-20</strong>. That tag belongs to myspafilter.com. We do not put any other Associates tag on these links. Two kinds of Amazon URL appear:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>A direct product link</strong> (<code>amazon.com/dp/…</code>) only when we have opened that listing and checked that the title shows the brand and part number we name. The cartridge page tells you which listing the button opens. The record of that check stays in the site data. We do not guess an ASIN.</li>
<li><strong>A search link</strong> (<code>amazon.com/s?k=…</code>) when we do not have a checked listing. The search is the part number plus “spa filter,” or a product name on a supplies guide. A search is not a promise that the first result is the right cartridge. Read the title, the size and the end fittings, and compare them with the cartridge page or your old filter.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not print dollar prices or star ratings. Both change, and we have not lab-tested the products. A “says” line under a named product repeats what the listing title said on the day we checked it, not a review.</p>
<h2>Other retailers</h2>
<p>FiltersFast and Doheny's buttons are searches for the same part number, so you can check another seller. They carry the same <code>rel</code> attributes. If an affiliate program ID is not configured, those buttons are ordinary search links with no tracking parameter. We do not invent an affiliate ID.</p>
<h2>What the links are not</h2>
<p>A retailer button is not a fit guarantee and not an endorsement by the spa manufacturer. Hot Spring, Jacuzzi and the filter catalogs do not write our pages. Availability, shipping, returns and the condition of the item are between you and the retailer. If a listing title does not show the part number on our page, do not assume it is that cartridge. The <a href="/guides/how-to-find-your-spa-filter-size/">size guide</a> and the <a href="/guides/open-end-vs-threaded-hot-tub-filters/">fitting guide</a> are the checks that matter before you order.</p>
<p>Questions about a link or a correction go to <a href="mailto:contact@myspafilter.com">contact@myspafilter.com</a>. That is the only address this site publishes. See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>
</Page>
